Which license applies to a given distribution

1. Zarya source (or builds) that do NOT link Desktop App Toolkit libraries
   (lib_ui, lib_base, and related desktop-app components) may be used under
   either the MIT License or GPLv3+, at your option.

2. Official and other builds that link Desktop App Toolkit (CMake option
   ZARYA_DESKTOP_APP_UI=ON, or any binary that includes those libraries) MUST
   be distributed under GPLv3+ (or a compatible license), because the Toolkit
   is licensed under GPLv3+ with an OpenSSL linking exception. See:

   https://github.com/desktop-app/legal/blob/master/LEGAL

3. Third-party components (Qt, Xray, sing-box, etc.) remain under their own
   licenses. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

